================================================================================
Changes made by the BioRadar team (required by Apache-2.0 Section 4b)
================================================================================

Provenance of the forked source
  The Snakemake pipeline was extracted from the published Docker image
  `dwheelerau/edna:v1.4`, at the path /home/docker_conda_template/
  snakemake-qiime-edna, rather than cloned from Bitbucket. The extracted tree
  is committed unmodified except where listed below. This route was chosen so
  the team owns a verifiable copy of the exact pipeline that the published,
  peer-reviewed image runs, independent of the upstream host's availability.

Additions
  * bioradar-pipeline/rules/bioradar.smk -- two new Snakemake rules:
      - normalize_taxonomy: converts raw QIIME2 output into BioRadar's frozen
        integration contract (see docs/CONTRACTS.md)
      - emit_hash: computes SHA-256 digests of the run's artifacts and commits
        them to BioRadar's chain-of-custody ledger
  * bioradar/ -- a new Python package providing the pipeline-to-backend
    integration layer (normalizer, programmatic runner, chain client,
    temporal comparison, mock-data generator). Original BioRadar work; no
    upstream code is reused.
  * docker-compose.yml, ci/, tests/, integration/, data/, docs/ -- original
    BioRadar work.

Modifications to upstream files
  * bioradar-pipeline/Snakefile -- `include:` added for rules/bioradar.smk, and
    `rule all` extended with three additional targets. The ten upstream rules
    and their input/output contracts are unchanged.

  * bioradar-pipeline/rules/*.smk -- `denoiser` switch added so a run can use
    vsearch (97% OTUs) instead of DADA2 when the input carries no usable
    quality scores; `fast` switch added so the PDF QC report and rarefaction
    can be skipped. Both default to upstream behaviour where behaviour matters.

Redistribution as a container image
  BioRadar publishes ghcr.io/omtawde09/bioradar-pipeline, built from
  docker/Dockerfile.pipeline with `dwheelerau/edna:v1.4` as its base. The
  derived image relocates the analysis assets to /opt/bioradar/ and carries a
  copy of this NOTICE and of LICENSE at /opt/bioradar/, so the attribution
  travels with the image and not only with this repository. Apache-2.0
  Section 4 permits this redistribution in modified form on exactly these
  terms.

Removals
  * The Flask web GUI (app.py, templates/, static/, the desktop launcher and
    install script) is not part of the BioRadar build and is not carried in
    this repository. BioRadar replaces it with its own web application. The
    upstream GUI remains available from the sources listed above.

Not modified
  The bioinformatics itself is upstream's and is deliberately untouched: the
  DADA2 denoising parameters, the cutadapt primer-trimming settings, the naive
  Bayes classification step, the rarefaction and report generation, and the
  order and dependencies of the ten original rules. BioRadar's contribution is
  the layer above the pipeline, not the pipeline.

